            <div xml:id="d425">

                <pb facs="0519" n="417" xml:id="pg417"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">817.51/1849: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in Nicaragua</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Munro</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Paraphrase]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Managua</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1927-11-01T12:00:00-05:45"><hi rendition="#italic">November 1,
                                1927—noon</hi></date>.<lb/>[Received 4:24 p.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>311. Department’s 167, October 28, 5 p.m. The proposal to send Cumberland to make
                    a financial survey meets with the hearty approval of both President Diaz and the
                    representatives of the Liberal Party. Will the Department or the Government of
                    Nicaragua bear the expenses?</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Munro</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
